  - emergent spacetime
  - Energy-Flow Cosmology
abstract: >-
  We formalise the regime structure underlying discrete entropic gravity models
  based on graph-defined functionals. Rather than treating gravitational
  dynamics as universally geometric, we show that distinct physical behaviours
  emerge from dominance transitions between gradient, bulk, and source sectors
  of a discrete entropic functional. The ultraviolet (strong-field), infrared
  (weak-field), and cosmological regimes arise naturally as scale-dependent
  responses of an entropic flow network. We clarify the ontological status of
  entropy, energy flow, and the cosmological constant within this framework,
  and demonstrate that Λ functions as a bulk capacity parameter governing
  large-scale screening. The analysis provides a regime-based foundation for
  discrete gravity models without assuming a fundamental spacetime metric.
